  "family": "Cupressaceae",
  "memo": "Although the Monterey cypress is among the most widely cultivated trees in the world, it's rare in the wild. It occurs naturally only on the foggy, windswept slopes near Pebble Beach and Carmel in Monterey County. Fossil records show that surviving stands are remnants of more extensive forests once growing along the west coast of North America. Old, unopened cones are visible on the branches, where they remain with their seeds enclosed until opened by the heat of a fire.",
